  "response": "```python\ndef dedupe_records(records):\n    \"\"\"\n    Deduplicate dict records by first id while preserving order;\n    missing id records are all retained; do not mutate.\n\n    Args:\n        records (list): A list of dictionaries with 'id' key.\n\n    Returns:\n        list: The deduplicated list of records.\n    \"\"\"\n    seen = set()\n    result = []\n    \n    for record in records:\n        if record['id'] not in seen:\n            seen.add(record['id'])\n            result.append(record)\n    \n    return result\n```\n\n示例使用：\n\n```python\nrecords = [\n    {'id': 1, 'name': 'John'},\n    {'id': 2, 'name': 'Jane'},\n    {'id': 3, 'name': 'Bob'},\n    {'id': 4, 'name': 'Alice'}\n]\n\ndeduplicated_records = dedupe_records(records)\nprint(deduplicated_records)  # [{'id': 1, 'name': 'John'}, {'id': 2, 'name': 'Jane'}, {'id': 3, 'name': 'Bob'}, {'id': 4, 'name': 'Alice'}]\n```\n\n在这个示例中，`dedupe_records` 函数接受一个列表 `records`，其中每个元素是字典。它使用一个集合 `seen` 来跟踪已经处理的 ID。对于每个记录，它检查是否已经在集合中存在。如果没有，则将其添加到集合中并将其添加到结果列表中。最终，函数返回一个不包含重复 ID 的列表。",
